*HEADING
A3c: as A3 with 16 mm beams of 4 elements (4 mm long, so Abaqus needs no contact-radius reduction: radius / edge length = 0.2 and 0.125); A clamped at both ends, B free at 2 m/s; frictionless
** Generated by abaqus/cases.py. Units: mm, N, s, tonne, MPa.
** Contact: general contact over all exterior. Beam elements enter as contact edges with a circular cross-section
** whose radius is the CIRC section radius (exact here). By default Abaqus/Explicit REDUCES contact thickness/radius
** where it is large compared with the edge length (first A3 run: radius x 0.375, warning in the .sta and element
** set WarnElemGContThickReduce), which let the beams overlap by ~a radius. CONTACT THICKNESS REDUCTION=NOPERIMSELF
** below restricts the reduction to regions of potential self-contact, so the full section radius is used.
** CHECK the .sta: there should be no 'contact edge thicknesses ... were reduced' warning (if there is, see A3c).
